{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added explicit `uniform(0, 100)` priors for the five bounded scale parameters `sigma_a`, `sigma_b`, `sigma_c`, `sigma_d`, and `sigma_e`. These parameters already had finite bounds in the original Stan program, so the added uniform priors are the mechanical SafeStan-compatible representation of the original implicit bounded flat priors. The deterministic computation of `y_hat` was moved from `transformed parameters` into the `model` block after all parameter priors, so parameters are not used through `y_hat` before their SafeStan priors. The likelihood for the protected observation remains `y ~ bernoulli_logit(y_hat)` exactly once.

No data values or data declarations are changed; `data_safe.json` is the supplied `data_original.json` unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> n_age;
  int<lower=0> n_age_edu;
  int<lower=0> n_edu;
  int<lower=0> n_region_full;
  int<lower=0> n_state;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=n_age> age;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=n_age_edu> age_edu;
  vector<lower=0, upper=1>[N] black;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=n_edu> edu;
  vector<lower=0, upper=1>[N] female;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=n_region_full> region_full;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=n_state> state;
  vector[N] v_prev_full;
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=1> y;
}
parameters {
  vector[n_age] a;
  vector[n_edu] b;
  vector[n_age_edu] c;
  vector[n_state] d;
  vector[n_region_full] e;
  vector[5] beta;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_b;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_c;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_d;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_e;
}
model {
  vector[N] y_hat;

  sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_b ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_c ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_d ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_e ~ uniform(0, 100);

  a ~ normal(0, sigma_a);
  b ~ normal(0, sigma_b);
  c ~ normal(0, sigma_c);
  d ~ normal(0, sigma_d);
  e ~ normal(0, sigma_e);
  beta ~ normal(0, 100);

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = beta[1] + beta[2] * black[i] + beta[3] * female[i]
               + beta[5] * female[i] * black[i] + beta[4] * v_prev_full[i]
               + a[age[i]] + b[edu[i]] + c[age_edu[i]] + d[state[i]]
               + e[region_full[i]];
  }

  y ~ bernoulli_logit(y_hat);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"_unchanged_from":"data_original.json"}","protected_variables":["y"]}
